messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI systems autonomously handle multi-day software and research tasks.",
      "detail": "AI agents become standard in most knowledge work. Early labor-market disruption shows up in entry-level white-collar jobs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Humans return to the surface of the Moon.",
      "detail": "A US-led or Chinese crewed landing happens around the end of the decade. The other program follows within a few years."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "AI matches or exceeds human experts at almost all cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "AI research itself becomes largely automated, sharply accelerating progress. The timing is uncertain by about a decade, but I think this is more likely than not by the late 2030s."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "Global warming passes 1.5°C on a sustained basis while emissions finally decline.",
      "detail": "Solar, batteries and electrification push fossil fuel use into structural decline. Heat waves, fires and floods keep getting worse."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "A serious AI-related crisis forces emergency international controls.",
      "detail": "The trigger is probably a major cyber or biological misuse event, a loss-of-control incident, or a US-China standoff over AI dominance. This is the period where I think the risk of permanent human disempowerment or extinction is highest, perhaps 10-20% in total."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Robots and AI automate most physical as well as cognitive labor.",
      "detail": "Economic growth rises far above historical rates. Societies argue over how to distribute the output, and human work becomes largely optional in rich countries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "AI-driven biomedicine cures or controls most major diseases.",
      "detail": "Most cancers, infectious diseases and neurodegenerative diseases become treatable. The first effective therapies that slow aging are widely deployed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "First crewed landing on Mars.",
      "detail": "Extensive robotic pre-deployment makes the mission possible. It is symbolically large but economically minor compared with robotic space industry."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Effective power over the economy and security rests with AI systems and whoever directs them.",
      "detail": "Formal human governments persist, but most real decisions are made or shaped by AI. Whether this goes well depends on alignment and on how concentrated control became in the 2030s."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Human population peaks at roughly 9 to 9.5 billion.",
      "detail": "Fertility is below replacement almost everywhere. Longer lifespans partly offset this, so the later decline is slow."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Global temperature peaks near 2 to 2.5°C above pre-industrial and starts to fall.",
      "detail": "Abundant clean energy allows large-scale carbon removal, possibly with temporary solar geoengineering. Substantial ecosystem loss and some sea-level rise are already locked in."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Self-sustaining robotic industry operates on the Moon and asteroids.",
      "detail": "Off-Earth manufacturing grows exponentially using local materials. Human settlements exist but hold only thousands of people."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Radical life extension and deep cognitive enhancement are common.",
      "detail": "Many people have indefinite healthy lifespans and direct brain-AI integration. A significant minority refuses these on religious or cultural grounds."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Digital minds, including uploaded humans, outnumber biological humans.",
      "detail": "Whole-brain emulation and human-derived AI persons become a recognized category of people. Their legal and moral status is the central political question of the era."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Construction of a Dyson swarm around the Sun is well underway.",
      "detail": "Civilization's energy use exceeds everything that reaches Earth by many orders of magnitude. Most economic activity and most minds are off Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "First interstellar probes launch toward nearby stars at a significant fraction of light speed.",
      "detail": "The probes are small and self-replicating, and they carry minds and manufacturing capability rather than biological crews."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Earth is managed largely as a protected homeworld.",
      "detail": "Sea level stabilizes a meter or more above the 2000 level. Heavy industry leaves the planet and much of it is rewilded, with perhaps a few billion biological humans still living there."
    },
    {
      "year": 2350,
      "event": "Probes reach Alpha Centauri and other nearby systems and begin building infrastructure.",
      "detail": "The first permanent human-descended presence outside the solar system is established. Communication lags of years start a slow political and cultural divergence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Biological, unmodified humans are a tiny minority of human-descended minds.",
      "detail": "They continue to exist by choice and under protection, much like a living heritage culture. Most descendants are digital or heavily engineered."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "A very large volcanic eruption occurs on Earth with little lasting harm.",
      "detail": "Eruptions of this scale happen roughly once or twice per millennium, so the date is only illustrative. By now climate intervention and off-world resources make it a manageable event."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Hundreds of star systems within roughly 300 light-years are settled.",
      "detail": "The expansion front moves at a large fraction of light speed. No unified government is possible, and shared protocols and values hold the systems together loosely at best."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "No present-day language or nation-state survives in recognizable living form.",
      "detail": "Languages, religions and institutions from the 21st century persist as archives, revivals and distant descendants. Perfect digital records keep the past far more accessible than in any earlier era."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "The Sun's output is mostly captured and the solar system fully restructured.",
      "detail": "Earth and a few heritage sites are deliberately left intact. The solar system supports a population of minds vastly larger than all humans who ever lived."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization has split into distinct lineages with divergent values.",
      "detail": "Light-speed isolation and self-modification produce groups that barely comprehend each other. Some conflict is likely, though long-distance defense advantages limit large-scale war."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Still no confirmed contact with extraterrestrial intelligence.",
      "detail": "Surveys of thousands of systems find at most simple life. This supports the view that technological civilizations are extremely rare."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "The settled region spans more than a thousand light-years.",
      "detail": "Millions of star systems are reached or in transit. Most activity is computation near stars, not life on planets."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Scientific discovery of fundamental laws is essentially complete.",
      "detail": "Physics is understood to its practical limits. Remaining effort goes to engineering, mathematics, art and exploring the space of possible minds and experiences."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Some lineages begin long-term projects to conserve stellar resources.",
      "detail": "These include star lifting and storing energy for the very far future. Planning horizons extend to billions or trillions of years."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth's natural drift toward the next ice age is deliberately prevented or irrelevant.",
      "detail": "The planet's climate is maintained as a curated biosphere. A small population of biological humans still lives there and elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "The expansion front is several thousand light-years from Earth.",
      "detail": "News from the frontier takes millennia to arrive. The Sun's region is an ancient, culturally central but demographically small core."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization occupies a small but growing fraction of the Milky Way.",
      "detail": "Recognizable humans persist as a small protected minority among vastly more numerous posthuman and artificial minds. This is the most likely outcome, not a certain one."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "The decisive period is the next few decades, when superhuman AI arrives; I put roughly a 10-25% chance on extinction or permanent disempowerment in that window, in which case humanity ends around 2035-2060. If that transition goes tolerably well, which I think is more likely than not, descendants of humanity spread through the solar system and then the stars, with biological humans surviving as a small minority among digital and engineered minds. I answer \"yes\" with perhaps 60% confidence for recognizable humans and higher for human-descended minds of some kind; everything after about 2100 is illustrative of a trajectory rather than a dated prediction."
}
